        <type>audio::TranscriptionResult</type>
        <definition>audio::TranscriptionResult themis::whisper::InMemoryWhisperTranscriber::transcribe</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::vector&lt; float &gt; &amp;, float) override</argsstring>
        <name>transcribe</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::whisper::InMemoryWhisperTranscriber::transcribe</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classthemis_1_1whisper_1_1_i_whisper_transcriber_1ae8bd3cfb125f5ff57b2d743af383306c">transcribe</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; float &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>pcm</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>float</type>
          <declname>sample_rate</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Transcribes the provided audio input into structured transcription data. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This core method uses the underlying Whisper model to process raw audio bytes and generate a comprehensive <computeroutput><ref refid="" kindref="compound">audio::TranscriptionResult</ref></computeroutput> object containing transcribed text, timestamps, and confidence scores for synchronization purposes. The <computeroutput>audioInput</computeroutput> must be correctly formed and contain valid audio data recognized by the system&apos;s backend.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>audioInput</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Reference to the audio data source; must not be empty or improperly formatted. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>std::true_type The successful transcription result object containing all necessary details. Throws an exception upon failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
